msgstr "T"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "℃"
msgstr "℃"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "中国极端最高气温49.6℃，出现在新疆的吐鲁番盆地。中国极端最低气温-52.3℃，出现在黑龙江省漠河。"
msgstr "China's extreme maximum temperature is 49.6℃, recorded in the Turpan Basin, Xinjiang. China's extreme minimum temperature is -52.3℃, recorded in Mohe, Heilongjiang Province."

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "气压"
msgstr "Atmospheric Pressure"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "海平面气压SLP"
msgstr "Sea Level Pressure SLP"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "kpa"
msgstr "kpa"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "由于大气的密度是不均匀的，随海拔的改变而有很大变化，但在近地面的空间可以认为近似不变的，几千米的海拔，范围内满足12mmHg/Km，即海拔每升高一千米，气压下降12毫米汞柱，以海拔0时的大气压为760mmHg，则某一海拔高度h的大气压强为P=760-h*12mmHg/Km。"
msgstr ""
"Since atmospheric density is non-uniform and varies greatly with altitude, but can be considered approximately constant in near-surface space. "
"Within an altitude range of several kilometers, it follows 12mmHg/Km, meaning atmospheric pressure drops by 12 mmHg for every 1,000 meters of altitude increase. "
"With sea level atmospheric pressure at 760mmHg, the atmospheric pressure at altitude h is P=760-h*12mmHg/Km."

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "降雨量"
msgstr "Rainfall"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "RF"
msgstr "RF"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "200mm"
msgstr "200mm"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "通常说的小雨、中雨、大雨、暴雨等，一般以日降雨量衡量。其中小雨指日降雨量在10毫米以下；中雨日降雨量为10~24.9毫米；大雨降雨量为25~49.9毫米；暴雨降雨量为50~99.9毫米；大暴雨降雨量为100~250毫米；特大暴雨降雨量在250毫米以上。"
msgstr ""
"The commonly mentioned light rain, moderate rain, heavy rain, torrential rain, etc. are generally measured by daily rainfall. "
"Light rain refers to daily rainfall below 10mm; moderate rain is 10-24.9mm; heavy rain is 25-49.9mm; torrential rain is 50-99.9mm; "
"severe torrential rain is 100-250mm; extraordinary torrential rain exceeds 250mm."

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "细颗粒物"
msgstr "Fine Particulate Matter"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "PM25"
msgstr "PM25"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "59μg/m³"
msgstr "59μg/m³"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "24小时PM2.5平均值标准值，优0~35μg/m³，良35~75μg/m³，轻度污染75~115μg/m³，中度污染115~150μg/m³，重度污染150~250μg/m³，严重污染大于250μg/m³及以上。"
msgstr ""
"24-hour PM2.5 average standard values: Excellent 0-35μg/m³, Good 35-75μg/m³, Light Pollution 75-115μg/m³, "
"Moderate Pollution 115-150μg/m³, Heavy Pollution 150-250μg/m³, Severe Pollution above 250μg/m³."

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "湿度"
msgstr "Humidity"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "RH"
msgstr "RH"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "80%"
msgstr "80%"

#: ../../source/gamedoc/gameplay/game0/ideas/battlefield-env.md:3
msgid "相对湿度表示空气中的水蒸气饱和值，取值范围为[0%,100%]。相对湿度通常与气温、气压共同作用于人体。现代医疗气象研究表明，对人体比较适宜的相对湿度为：夏季室温25℃时，相对湿度控制在40%－50%比较舒适；冬季室温20℃时，相对湿度控制在60%－70%。夏季三伏时节，由于高温、低压、高湿的作用，人体汗液不易排出，出汗后不易被蒸发掉，因而会使人烦躁、疲倦、食欲不振；冬季湿度有时太小，空气过于干燥，易引起上呼吸道粘膜感染，患上感冒。据科学试验，在气温日际变化大于3℃、气压日际变化大于10百帕，相对湿度日际变化大于10%时，关节炎的发病率会显著增加。"
msgstr ""
"Relative humidity represents the water vapor saturation value in the air, with a range of [0%, 100%]. Relative humidity typically affects the human body in conjunction with air temperature and atmospheric pressure. "
"Modern medical meteorology research indicates that relatively comfortable humidity levels for the human body are: 40%-50% at a summer room temperature of 25℃; 60%-70% at a winter room temperature of 20℃. "
"During the summer dog days, due to high temperature, low pressure, and high humidity, sweat is not easily expelled and hard to evaporate, causing irritability, fatigue, and loss of appetite. "
"In winter, humidity may be too low and the air too dry, easily causing upper respiratory mucosal infections and colds. "
"According to scientific experiments, when daily temperature variation exceeds 3℃, daily atmospheric pressure variation exceeds 10 hPa, and daily relative humidity variation exceeds 10%, the incidence of arthritis increases significantly."

